# Feature Workflow

## Scope
Defines the repeatable process for adding a new feature to the template or an app built from it.

## Mandatory rules
- Start every feature by identifying its route, state, data needs, validation, localization, responsive behavior, and tests.
- Create the feature folder using the standard `data/domain/presentation` structure.
- Define domain models and repository contracts before wiring UI to real data sources when the flow is non-trivial.
- Add localization keys before adding user-facing text to widgets.
- Use shared components before creating feature-specific widgets.
- Queue/workspace features must confirm layout against [`ui-workspace.mdc`](./ui-workspace.mdc) and a reference module before implementation.
- Confirm subscription-gated module access and permission gates before exposing routes or actions ([`permissions.mdc`](./permissions.mdc)).
- Deliver high-performance, uniform, simple, intuitive workflows; reuse `frontend/lib/shared/` components and verify mobile, tablet, and desktop layouts.
- Prohibit hard-coded color values, spacing values, and typography — use design tokens exclusively ([`design-system.mdc`](./design-system.mdc)).
- Frontend must reference entities by `human_friendly_id`; backend maps to internal IDs. Do not expose raw table IDs in frontend or API responses.
- Menus, UI components, and workflow actions must never be visible or accessible to unauthorized users — enforce RBAC and ABAC visibility.
- Shared-data mutations must update Riverpod immediately and reconcile with backend realtime events per [`instant_ui_sync.mdc`](./instant_ui_sync.mdc).
- Add tests for controller logic, repository mapping, and important widgets.
- Update docs when the feature changes app structure or conventions.

## Implementation standard
- Small purely presentational features may omit use cases but must keep boundaries clear.
- Feature changes should be reviewable by files with focused responsibilities.

## Acceptance checklist
- The feature works at supported breakpoints.
- No architecture boundary is violated.
- Queue screens match [`ui-workspace.mdc`](./ui-workspace.mdc) when applicable.
- Tests and localization are included.

